Dijit,

Thanks for giving the experimental launchers a try. At the very least rJava\jri\JRI.jar should be present on any non-currupt install of rJava. I'm not sure exactly where etc\classes\classes.jar get generated (not by JGR though), but my understanding was that it should be present in any installation with shared objects (perhaps Simon could provide insight here). Some additional information will help debug the problem.

1. Was JGR working for you prior to upgrading to the experimental JGR 1.7-16?

2. What is the result of:

library(JGR)
R.home()
.libPaths()
sessionInfo()

3. Do you get the same issue trying to launch from 32-bit R, loadable with something like: R -arch=32

4. Did you try the jgr2.exe launcher in step 3 of  http://mailman.rz.uni-augsburg.de/pipermail/stats-rosuda-devel/2013q3/002057.html?

5. What version of Java do you have? You can get this with:

library(rJava)
J("java.lang.System")$getProperty("java.version")

best,
Ian


